  "created": "2026-11-11T19:19:39.61Z",
  "description": "HiQPdf Next Word to PDF Converter for .NET (Multi-platform) is a component of the HiQPdf Next Library for .NET that enables accurate conversion of complex Word documents to PDF.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows, Linux and macOS, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis multi-platform metapackage installs the Windows x64 and Linux x64 runtimes.\n\nFor Windows ARM64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64, the additional packages HiQPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.WordToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.WordToPdf.MacOS can be referenced on their own or alongside this package.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 10, 11 and Windows Server 2016 to 2025 (x64)\n* Linux (x64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* Windows, Linux and macOS (ARM64) - via additional packages\n* .NET 11.0, 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* .NET Framework 4.6.2 to 4.8.1\n* Azure, AWS and Google Cloud\n* Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert Word DOCX documents from memory or from file to PDF\n* Use the PDF page settings from the original Word document\n* Use custom PDF page settings to automatically reflow the content\n* Automatically create a table of contents based on headings in Word\n* Use the page break marks from Word\n* Add HTML headers, footers or stamps to the generated PDF\n* Control the PDF document display with PDF viewer preferences\n* Encrypt, set permissions and set passwords for the generated PDF documents\n* Add digital signatures to the generated PDF document\n* Asynchronous methods for async and await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-next-word-docx-to-pdf-dotnet",
